From 0463fee3d8dd49832cc2e1405e54560c3ac695f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 09:57:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] libretech-ac.conf: honour the cortexa53-nocrypto tune

S805X is Amlogic GXL (Cortex-A53) without the ARMv8 crypto extensions,
same silicon gap as BCM2837. amlogic-s905x.inc pulls in
tune-cortexa53.inc, which defaults DEFAULTTUNE to plain "cortexa53"
(crypto-capable codegen) before this file gets a chance to say
otherwise. Claim cortexa53-nocrypto here first, matching how
meta-raspberrypi's raspberrypi3-64.conf handles the same situation for
BCM2837 -- a downstream distro that forces a -crypto tune onto
whatever TUNE_FEATURES implies (Angstrom's arm_tune_handler does
exactly this) would otherwise put SIGILL-triggering AES/SHA
instructions into every binary on real hardware.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
---
 conf/machine/libretech-ac.conf | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/conf/machine/libretech-ac.conf b/conf/machine/libretech-ac.conf
index 0c39d05..6815bdc 100644
--- a/conf/machine/libretech-ac.conf
+++ b/conf/machine/libretech-ac.conf
@@ -2,6 +2,11 @@
 #@NAME: LibreTech AC (AML-S805X-AC La Frite) machine
 #@DESCRIPTION: Machine configuration for USB bootable image
 
+# S805X (Amlogic GXL) has no ARMv8 crypto extensions; claim the -nocrypto
+# tune before tune-cortexa53.inc's own default runs, same pattern as
+# meta-raspberrypi's raspberrypi3-64.conf (BCM2837, same silicon gap).
+DEFAULTTUNE ?= "cortexa53-nocrypto"
+
 require conf/machine/include/amlogic-s905x.inc
 require conf/machine/include/libretech-ac-dtb.inc
 require conf/machine/include/amlogic-modern-boot.inc
